Version @(#) $Id: ChangeLog.patches,v 1.15 2002/11/21 19:07:02 dl9sau Exp $

021121 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>
	- login.c and doc/wampes.*, doc/intro.txt
		- home directory "funk" for amateur radio packet users is a
		  bit confusing for non-german users. /home/hams/ may be a
		  better approach
		
021019 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	- krnlif.c
		- bugfix. sent only one packet even if several packets were
	    	  in queue.
		- interface labeling. now:
		    attach kernel <iface> [label] [nopromisc]
		  also changed config.c for this

020920 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

        - patch for ARP requests (to QST-0) via multible digipeaters
	  for an extended "collision domain". changed iface.c and ax25.c.
	  examples:
	    ifconfig linuxBPQ digiarp add db0tud  # arp directly to db0tud
	    ifconfig linuxBPQ digiarp add -       # no direct ARPs
	    ifconfig linuxBPQ digiarp addvia db0tud  # arp to QST-0 via db0tud
	- builtin smtp client now capable of taylor uucp spool formats
	  and bsmtp encoded spool files
	- version.c:
	  added DIGIARP feature

020918 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>
	- bugfix in ax25cmd.c's VJ part:
                ax_routeptr(hdr.dest, 1); is right, not ".., 0)"
                this caused a segfault in ax ro add qst
                (which is not valid due to other reasons, but caused a
                race condition)
	- ax25dump.c:
		trace on ax25 interfaces now displays DAMA flag
	- krnlif.c:
       		- fix in error message
        	- added params to krnlif_ioctl, like in kiss.c/kiss_ioctl()

	- util/qth.c:
		- added nmea GPGGA conform output
        	- Gauss-Krueger coordinaties now a possible input format
          	  (gk locators are transmitted for e.g. as CellBroadcast by
		  German mobile-TK-providers like O2 (ex Viag Interkomm))

020619 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	- fix in krnlif.c:
	  forgot to close socket on error during attach
	- ethertap.c:
	  - now with the generic TUN/TAP driver support for kernel >= 2.4.x
	    linux kernel doku: the classic ethertap device (/dev/tapX)
	      is obsolete and will be removed soon. tun/tap uses /dev/net/tun
	  - now supports rx/tx BPQether protocol (ax25-over-ethernet)
	    the bpqether device generated automaticaly:
	      "attach ethertap linux" becomes linux and linuxBPQ
	    this is a more efficient way than attaching an mkiss device
	    to a pseudo-tty for the link between kernel-ax25 and wampes.
	  - cave MTU: there seems to be a bug. mtu = 1500 has a throughput
	    of 9k6 bit/s. mtu = 1024 makes ca. 1Mbit -> you may use the new mtu
	    arg when attaching an ethertap device
	  - on attach, we now probe the hardware-address (MAC) of the device.
	    this is needed because tun/tap accepts only correctly addressed
	    packets.
	- config.c:
	  attach ethertap now with optional MTU argument
	- version.c:
	  added TUN/TAP feature

020614 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	- fix in nrdump.c:
	  trace for announced netrom broadcasts should show quality
	  (linux / GCC problem?). instead the address of &tmp was shown.

020527 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	- fix in route.c / rip_route():
	    rt_add() may return 0 in some conditions, so rp is NULL.
	    will log this event (when trace is on).
	- added support for linux on sparc10 (sun4m)

020205 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	added "axp->r_upcall = axserv_recv_upcall_discard;" instead of
	"disc_ax25(axp);" to axserver.c, in order not to disc the ax25
	layer while transports with other PIDs are open

020123 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	added comments and my name to the code where changes to the
	original were made - for better reference

020122 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	software like xnet always sends PID=text CText on ax25 connects.
	a connect from wampes to an xnet triggered by an IP frame that
	is routed as AX25.IP VC leaded to a login of the xnet to our
	own system due to the received CText (or to a disconnect if login
	is disabled)
	a modification in ax25.c now fixes this problem with non-protocol-
	compliant hosts like xnet.

020112 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

	mail_smtp.c had problems on ax25 smtp (where \r\n is sent as \r\r,
	which results in an empty line.
	additionaly, while profile is running, the cmd.smtp command may
	get lost. now sending \n in a seperate packet before
	issuing cmd.smtp

010213 Thomas Osterried <dl9sau>

        providing patches for wampes-000304:

        I. AX25-tcp-van-jacobsen-compression
                written by Matthias Welwarsky, DG2FEF
                modified by me to be activated with -DAX25_VJCOMP

        II. krnlif.c modification for linux-kernel 2.2 compatibility
            force the old behaviour with -DUSE_OBSOLETE_SOCK_PACKET
